@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nii-il04-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il04-published-figures`
IMPORT `nii-s1-definitions`
IMPORT `nii-s334-interpretation`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-j-tables`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-j`
IMPORT `nii-s337-rates`

-- INDEPENDENT TESTS for row IL-04, by fid-il-04 (one session, no sub-agents).
--
-- Every expected value here was decided from the Hebrew source BEFORE this author opened any .l4
-- file, NOTES.md, encoding.json, check.sh or tools/ of this encoding. The decisions, with the
-- provisions and Hebrew words that license each, are in DECIDED-ANSWERS.md (stamped with the
-- time it was finished); scenario ids below (V1, T3, E5, ...) are its ids. The encoding was read
-- afterwards only to learn its exported names and how inputs are supplied. The encoder's own
-- tests modules were not used for expected values.
--
-- An assertion that FAILS here is a finding, and is left failing. INDEPENDENT-FINDINGS.md lists
-- every one with its classification.
--
-- The cell assertions (section 2 of DECIDED-ANSWERS) are generated by a script from the cell
-- data this author typed from the source before opening the encoding; the scenarios below them
-- are hand-written.

§ `Independent tests`

§§ `Helpers: the version a year selects, an item of it, and the input records`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A version of Schedule J`
`ind v` y MEANS `Schedule J — the version for a contribution month in` y

GIVEN v IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A row of Schedule J`
`ind row` v n MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `item` EQUALS n) (v's `rows`)
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN r
    OTHERWISE REFUSE "fid-il-04 test helper: no such item"

-- Every branch an employee's column prints a figure for (items 1, 3-10): DECIDED-ANSWERS s 5.
`ind all employee branches` MEANS
    LIST `maternity`, `children`, `work injury`, `accident injury`, `unemployment`
       , `employees' rights in insolvency proceedings`, `disability`, `long-term care`
       , `senior citizens and survivors`

-- Items 1, 3, 4, 5, 8, 9, 10: DECIDED-ANSWERS s 6, and K16 (a controlling shareholder of a close
-- company, who is excused items 6 and 7 by s 335(e)-(f), an input here).
`ind seven branches` MEANS
    LIST `maternity`, `children`, `work injury`, `accident injury`, `disability`, `long-term care`
       , `senior citizens and survivors`

-- Items 2, 3, 5, 8, 9, 10: DECIDED-ANSWERS s 7.
`ind neither branches` MEANS
    LIST `maternity`, `children`, `accident injury`, `disability`, `long-term care`
       , `senior citizens and survivors`

-- The branches whose column D prints a figure (items 1, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10): DECIDED-ANSWERS s 12.
`ind deduction branches` MEANS
    LIST `maternity`, `accident injury`, `unemployment`, `disability`, `long-term care`
       , `senior citizens and survivors`

GIVEN y  IS A NUMBER
      w  IS A NUMBER
      bs IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
GIVETH AN `An employee's month of contributions`
`ind month` y w bs MEANS
    `An employee's month of contributions` WITH
        `calendar year of the month`                                          IS y
        `branches for which contributions are payable under section 335`      IS bs
        `monthly income on which contributions are computed`                  IS w
        `reduced rates under an order made under section 341 apply to this income` IS FALSE
        `the employer pays reduced work-injury contributions under section 343` IS FALSE

GIVEN y      IS A NUMBER
      c      IS A `The Schedule J column of an insured person who is not an employee`
      annual IS A NUMBER
      n      IS A NUMBER
      bs     IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
GIVETH AN `Another insured person's year of contributions`
`ind year` y c annual n bs MEANS
    `Another insured person's year of contributions` WITH
        `calendar year`                                                       IS y
        `column`                                                              IS c
        `branches for which contributions are payable under section 335`      IS bs
        `annual income on which contributions are computed`                   IS annual
        `number of periods set for paying advances`                           IS n
        `reduced rates under an order made under section 341 apply to this income` IS FALSE

GIVEN employed IS A BOOLEAN
      family   IS A BOOLEAN
      regular  IS A BOOLEAN
      otherwise IS A BOOLEAN
      fixed    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A person who works`
`ind worker` employed family regular otherwise fixed MEANS
    `A person who works` WITH
        `employed within an employment relationship`                          IS employed
        `a parent, child, grandchild, brother or sister of the relative employing them` IS family
        `works in the enterprise regularly`                                   IS regular
        `in work which, had they not done it, would have been done by an employee` IS otherwise
        `wage fixed in a Law or in or under a resolution of the Knesset`      IS fixed

GIVEN notemployee IS A BOOLEAN
      hours       IS A NUMBER
      income      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A person's occupation in a period`
`ind occupation` notemployee hours income MEANS
    `A person's occupation in a period` WITH
        `engaged in the period in an occupation not as an employee`           IS notemployee
        `average hours a week in the occupation`                               IS hours
        `average monthly income from the occupation`                           IS income

-- K7-K14 use the 2026 average wage 13,566 and an invented Schedule A sum of 2,000 (DECIDED s 0).
GIVEN o IS A `A person's occupation in a period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind self-employed` o MEANS
    `s 1 — a self-employed person in the period:` o `with the average wage at` 13566 `and the Schedule A sum at` 2000

GIVEN m1 IS A NUMBER
      m2 IS A NUMBER
      m3 IS A NUMBER
      cr IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The data for an update of the average wage`
`ind wage data` m1 m2 m3 cr MEANS
    `The data for an update of the average wage` WITH
        `CBS average wage per employee post, first of the three months`                IS m1
        `CBS average wage per employee post, second of the three months`               IS m2
        `CBS average wage per employee post, third of the three months`                IS m3
        `compensation rate given from the end of those three months to the update day` IS cr

GIVEN minister  IS A BOOLEAN
      approved  IS A BOOLEAN
      bs        IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
      consulted IS A BOOLEAN
      consented IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An order changing the rates in Schedule J`
`ind order` minister approved bs consulted consented MEANS
    `An order changing the rates in Schedule J` WITH
        `made by the Minister`                                                IS minister
        `approved by the Finance Committee of the Knesset`                    IS approved
        `branches whose rates it changes`                                     IS bs
        `made after consultation with the Minister of Finance`                IS consulted
        `made with the consent of the Minister of Finance`                    IS consented

