§§ `DECIDED-ANSWERS section 11 — s 337(b) and (c)`

-- M1 is the cell section: no order is applied on top of the printed rates.
-- M2: item 10, employee above T, 5.89 -> 6.00 carries D-upper 1.52 to 1.52 x 6.00/5.89 = 48/31
#ASSERT `s 337(c) — the deduction of` 1.52 `after the rate changes from` 5.89 `to` 6.00 EQUALS (48 DIVIDED BY 31)
-- M3: item 3 (children), column D is a dash: there is no deduction to scale
#ASSERT REFUSED `the percentage in column D of` (`ind v` 2028) `for` `children` `in` `column D, upper part of the wage`
-- M4: who may make the order, and the two provisos
#ASSERT `s 1 — "the Minister"` EQUALS "the Minister of Labour and Welfare"
#ASSERT `s 337(b) — the order is within the Minister's power` (`ind order` TRUE TRUE (LIST `senior citizens and survivors`) FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 337(b) — the order is within the Minister's power` (`ind order` TRUE FALSE (LIST `senior citizens and survivors`) FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 337(b) — the order is within the Minister's power` (`ind order` FALSE TRUE (LIST `senior citizens and survivors`) FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 337(b) — the order is within the Minister's power` (`ind order` TRUE TRUE (LIST `employees' rights in insolvency proceedings`) FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 337(b) — the order is within the Minister's power` (`ind order` TRUE TRUE (LIST `employees' rights in insolvency proceedings`) TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 337(b) — the order is within the Minister's power` (`ind order` TRUE TRUE (LIST `long-term care`) TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 337(b) — the order is within the Minister's power` (`ind order` TRUE TRUE (LIST `long-term care`) FALSE TRUE)

