-- NOTE BY THE LEAD, 2026-10-08 (not the independent tester's words; BACKLOG IL-21, inventory
-- 04-TF3, IL-04 v0.4.1). The five failures this file still has are the F3 expectations at lines
-- 756, 924 and 929-931. (T7 at line 787, the sixth failure the note above names, passes from
-- IL-04 v0.4.0, a fall in the index being declined by default.) The five follow the heading the
-- consolidation prints over the temporary table's column D upper part (source line 4718, "on the
-- part of the wage above 60% of the average wage"). The enacted Laws say otherwise for 2026: the
-- 2025 Budget-year Law, 5785-2025 (Sefer HaChukim 3384, pp. 395-396), s 19(6), replaces "60% of
-- the average wage" with "the reduced collection threshold as defined in section 334(a)"
-- everywhere in Schedule J, and s 21 commences it on 1 January 2026. So in 2026 column D's upper
-- part begins at the reduced collection threshold, 7,703, not at 60% of 13,566 (8,139.6): the
-- flag at line 756 is FALSE, line 924's figure is 7,703, and the wages at lines 929-931 (7,703.01,
-- 8,000 and 10,000) are answered, not refused. Worked by hand from column D's figures for these
-- branches (1.04 up to the threshold; above it the items 4.67, the printed total 7.00), they are
-- 80.111667, 93.9811 and 187.3811 on the items, the reading this author decided, and 80.1119,
-- 100.9012 and 240.9012 at the printed totals, the row's default since the F4 ruling. The
-- capstone's independent tester (row IL-07, fid-il-07), deciding from the Hebrew sources and the
-- amending Laws before opening any encoding, reached the 7,703 boundary separately from the same
-- s 19(6) and s 21 (its DECIDED-ANSWERS.md line 69; its INDEPENDENT-FINDINGS.md line 41: "the
-- boundary is 7,703, not 8,139.60"). The five are kept as written, no expected value and no input
-- changed, and keep failing as the record of what the consolidation says; check.sh declares them
-- (expected_failed 5). Nothing was added above this note, so every line number still holds.
